'''Celestial Guardians''' (Japanese: '''{{j|双天の守護者}}''' ''Dual Sky Guardians'') is the third main expansion of cards in [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]].

== Information ==
'''Celestial Guardians''' is the third main expansion released through [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]]. The expansion focuses heavily on [[Generation VII]] and features Pokémon and characters from the [[Alola]] region, including Legendary Pokémon {{p|Solgaleo}} and {{p|Lunala}}, all [[Alolan form]]s introduced in the games, and all but one of the [[Trial Captain]]s. Its two booster packs are themed around {{p|Solgaleo}} and {{p|Lunala}}, the [[game mascot]]s and featured Legendary Pokémon of {{g|Sun and Moon}}.

The expansion also features the game's first {{TCGP|immersive card|immersive}} {{TCG|Supporter card}}s, {{TCG ID|Celestial Guardians|Guzma|208}} and {{TCG ID|Celestial Guardians|Lillie|209}}.

Several of the [[#Themed Collections|Themed Collections]] made available alongside Celestial Guardians also reference elements of Alola and the Generation VI games:
* '''Daytime Pack and Nighttime Pack''' features {{p|Yungoos}} and Alolan {{p|Rattata}}, which [[Evolution|evolve]] during the day and night respectively;
* '''Evolution Split by Day and Night''' features {{p|Rockruff}} alongside {{p|Lycanroc}} in both its Midday Form and Midnight Form;
* '''Alolan Dancers''' features {{p|Oricorio}} in its Baile Style, Pom-Pom Style, Pa'u Style, and Sensu Style;
* '''Captains of the Alola Region''' features six of the [[Trial Captain]]s found in the Alola region;
* '''Team Skull's Nasty Plot''' features [[Team Skull]] leader [[Guzma]] and his {{p|Golisopod}} alongside some Pokémon commonly used by Team Skull members;
* '''Lillie and Nebby's Growth''' features [[Lillie]] and her {{p|Cosmog}}, [[Nebby]], alongside its Evolutions;
* '''Guardian Deities of the Four Islands''' features the four [[guardian deities]], or tapu, of Alola's four islands;
* '''Standing Before You: Totem Pokémon''' features eight [[Totem Pokémon]] used by the Trial Captains;
* '''An Assembly of Alolan Forms''' features all 18 [[Alolan form]]s across two collections.

Additionally, the six Trial Captains featured in the set each have their own Themed Collection alongside some of the Pokémon they use in battles and trials, as well as some of their Totem Pokémon.

